59
00:03:24.583 --> 00:03:27.677
Your turn. Say: Validation-seeking.

60
00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:32.637
Validation-seeking.

61
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:34.791
Genuine connection.

62
00:03:35.783 --> 00:03:38.967
Genuine connection means a real, honest relationship.

63
00:03:39.583 --> 00:03:42.221
Genuine connection matters more than followers.

64
00:03:42.817 --> 00:03:45.887
Your turn. Say: Genuine connection.

65
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:50.199
Genuine connection.

66
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.628
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:55.483 --> 00:03:58.156
Visal, how does social media affect you?

68
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.421
Social media can make people feel pressured to compare themselves.

69
00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:05.785
Does it ever help?

70
00:04:06.883 --> 00:04:11.811
Yes. It lets me share my art and connect with other artists.

71
00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:14.568
How do you stay positive?

72
00:04:15.683 --> 00:04:20.147
I don't let likes control my mood. I make myself take breaks.

73
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.707
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.803
Grammar focus: Causative verbs (make and let).

75
00:04:27.103 --> 00:04:28.174
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:31.417
Social media can make people feel pressured.

77
00:04:32.317 --> 00:04:34.026
It lets me share my art.

78
00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:36.916
I don't let likes control my mood.

79
00:04:37.867 --> 00:04:43.807
'Make' means force or cause. 'Let' means allow. After both, use the base verb without 'to'.

80
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:49.211
Be careful! Don't say: Social media makes people to feel pressured.

81
00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:54.525
Say: Social media makes people feel pressured.

82
00:04:54.825 --> 00:04:57.289
After 'make' and 'let', don't use 'to'.

83
00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.659
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.445
The Real Me.

85
00:05:02.745 --> 00:05:06.079
Social media plays a big part in identity formation.

86
00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:10.622
Filtered reality can make teenagers feel self-image pressure.

87
00:05:11.633 --> 00:05:15.432
Comparison culture lets people judge themselves too harshly.

88
00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:19.083
A curated image is not the authentic self.

89
00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:23.262
Genuine connection matters more than validation-seeking.

90
00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:28.171
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:29.017 --> 00:05:30.703
It makes me blank happy.

92
00:05:31.003 --> 00:05:34.331
A, feel. B, to feel. C, feeling.

93
00:05:37.867 --> 00:05:39.448
The answer is A: feel.

94
00:05:40.583 --> 00:05:42.432
The real you is your blank self.

95
00:05:42.732 --> 00:05:46.223
A, authentic. B, digital. C, curated.

96
00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.789
The answer is A: authentic.

97
00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.227
Life that looks better than it really is is a blank reality.

98
00:05:56.527 --> 00:05:59.855
A, filtered. B, genuine. C, personal.

99
00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.237
The answer is A: filtered.

100
00:06:06.433 --> 00:06:09.666
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:10.517 --> 00:06:14.165
How does social media affect how teenagers see themselves?

102
00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.392
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:24.692 --> 00:06:34.705
Social media can make teenagers feel they are not good enough. I let myself use it for one hour a day, and I remind myself that many photos are filtered.

104
00:06:35.005 --> 00:06:36.599
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:37.483 --> 00:06:42.284
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and causative verbs (make and let).

106
00:06:42.584 --> 00:06:46.977
Today's value is self-acceptance. Big or little, you are special.

107
00:06:47.277 --> 00:06:49.872
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

108
00:06:50.172 --> 00:06:54.136
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

